1
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:36,000
Be Afraid is a horror, mystery, thriller film directed by Drew Gabreski.

2
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:06,000
Not long after John Chambers and his family arrive at their new home in a small
country town of Pennsylvania, John begins to experience sleep paralysis.

3
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:36,000
Lying there paralyzed, trapped within his own
nightmare, other-worldly beings visit John.

4
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:06,000
They are entities which exist in the darkest shadows of the night
and can only be seen out of the corner of one's eye.

5
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:36,000
These encounters begin to haunt John, transforming to complete
terror as he discovers the entities' sole purpose...

6
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:06,000
the abduction of his seven year old son.

7
00:31:30,000 --> 00:31:36,000
In the end, John will uncover the town's horrific secret, a portal on his land, and make one last
attempt to save his son before the shadow people permanently take him away to their world.

8
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Dr. John Chambers, played by Brian Krause.

9
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:36,000
Heather Chambers, played by Jaimi Paige.

10
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Chief Collins, played by Louis Herthum.

11
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:36,000
Ben Chambers, played by Jared Abrahamson.

12
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
Christine Booth, played by Michelle Hurd.

13
00:58:30,000 --> 00:58:36,000
Nathan Chambers, played by Michael Leone.

14
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
Beau Is Afraid is a 2023 American epic surrealist tragicomedy horror
film written, directed, and co-produced by Ari Aster.

15
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:36,000
The film stars Joaquin Phoenix as the title character, and also includes a supporting cast consisting of Patti LuPone, Nathan Lane, Amy Ryan, Kylie
Rogers, Parker Posey, Stephen McKinley Henderson, Hayley Squires, Michael Gandolfini, Zoe Lister-Jones, Armen Nahapetian, and Richard Kind.

16
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
Its plot follows the mild-mannered but paranoia-ridden Beau as he embarks on a surreal odyssey
to get home to his mother's house, realizing his greatest fears along the way.

17
01:16:30,000 --> 01:16:36,000
Distributed by A24, Beau Is Afraid premiered at the Alamo Drafthouse Cinema on April 1, 2023, and began a limited
theatrical release in the United States on April 14, 2023, before a wide release the following week.

18
01:21:00,000 --> 01:21:06,000
The film received generally positive reviews from critics but was a box-office bomb,
grossing $12 million against a net production cost of $35 million.

19
01:25:30,000 --> 01:25:36,000
Phoenix received a Golden Globe nomination for his performance.

20
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
The film explores themes of suicide, pennsylvania, usa,
loss of loved one, murder, shadowy figures.

21
01:34:30,000 --> 01:34:36,000
The tone is intense and dark and mind_bending.
